 ('frz8', "A state, it argues, is healthy only when all seven are. Its other famous idea is the mandala theory of foreign policy: your neighbour is your likely enemy, and your neighbour's neighbour is your likely friend."),
 ('plq1', "A caution about the book. Some scholars treat it as substantially Kautilya's, written in the Mauryan period, and read Mauryan administration directly out of it."),
